{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1030","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1030","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1030\",\"parent_revision\":\"b626d74551a5d0b9d58e6db36e322ba28d5fd9308da545c900e68f45faa33dbd\",\"root_revision\":\"b626d74551a5d0b9d58e6db36e322ba28d5fd9308da545c900e68f45faa33dbd\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPer Anthropic hook-development/references/advanced.md: multi-stage validation (combining command + prompt hooks), conditional hook execution (CI vs local, user-specific rules), hook chaining via state (temporary files to share context between hooks). plugin-creator mentions patterns but lacks consolidated \\\"advanced techniques\\\" section. Users would need to read multiple references to assemble this knowledge. Affected skills: hooks-patterns, hooks-core-reference.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Docs gap that affects every developer building advanced hook setups. The three missing patterns (multi-stage validation, conditional execution, hook chaining) are each individually useful but together form the foundation for production-grade hook systems. Without a consolidated section, developers must reverse-engineer these patterns from scattered examples or fail to discover them at all.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: developers who need multi-stage validation (e.g., command check followed by LLM review) from finding the pattern without reading multiple skills\\n- Bottleneck: hooks-patterns covers individual hook types well but has no section explaining how to combine them; hooks-core-reference covers events and config but no composition patterns\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Users building CI-aware hooks can find the conditional execution pattern without reading all hook docs\\n- Users implementing multi-step validation workflows can find the command+prompt chaining pattern in one place\\n- Users needing cross-hook state sharing (temp file pattern) have a documented, tested approach\\n- Reduces support load from users who currently must stitch together patterns from multiple skills\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nA developer reading hooks-patterns finds a dedicated 'Advanced Hook Patterns' section containing three sub-sections: multi-stage validation (command hook + prompt hook combined), conditional execution (CI vs local, user-specific rules via environment variables), and hook chaining via state (temporary files shared between hooks). Each sub-section shows a complete, working configuration and script example. The developer can copy the pattern and adapt it without needing to read any other skill.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nhooks-patterns gains a new top-level section 'Advanced Hook Patterns' with three subsections, each containing:\\n- A one-paragraph description of when to use the pattern\\n- A complete JSON hook configuration example\\n- A Python or bash script example demonstrating the implementation\\n- A note on which events/hook types are combined\\n\\nhooks-core-reference gains a cross-reference pointer to the advanced patterns section in hooks-patterns (the core reference currently has no mention of combining hook types).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. hooks-patterns/SKILL.md contains a section titled 'Advanced Hook Patterns' (or equivalent heading)\\n2. The multi-stage validation pattern is documented: a single hook event that runs a command hook first and a prompt hook second, with the command hook able to short-circuit the prompt hook on exit code 2\\n3. The conditional execution pattern is documented: a hook script that checks CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE or a custom env variable to skip or alter behavior in CI vs local environments\\n4. The hook chaining via state pattern is documented: two hooks on different events that communicate via a temporary file (e.g., PreToolUse writes state, PostToolUse reads it)\\n5. hooks-core-reference/SKILL.md cross-references the advanced patterns section in hooks-patterns\\n6. All code examples are syntactically valid (JSON config + script body)\\n7. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-patterns` exits 0 after changes\\n8. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-core-reference` exits 0 after changes\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-patterns \u2014 primary target skill, file: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-patterns/SKILL.md |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-core-reference \u2014 secondary target, cross-reference addition: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-core-reference/SKILL.md |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-io-api \u2014 JSON I/O schemas for hooks, useful for validating pattern examples: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-io-api/SKILL.md |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-guide \u2014 cross-platform hooks reference with best-practices: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-guide/references/best-practices.md |\\n| Prior work | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/hooks-patterns/SKILL.md \u2014 existing prompt hook + command hook examples that advanced patterns build on (lines 260\u2013310 show the two-layer UserPromptSubmit pattern, a partial precedent for multi-stage) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 hooks-patterns and hooks-core-reference are standalone; no other items need to complete first\\n- Blocks: None identified in open backlog\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 three new subsections added to one skill, one cross-reference line added to a second skill. All content is documentation-only with no code changes to scripts or plugin.json. Estimated: 1\u20132 hours of focused writing plus linting.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-24T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer reading the documentation**, I want to **plugin-creator gap: advanced hook patterns consolidation \u2014 missing from hook/agent skills** so that **documentation is accurate and trustworthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-24T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: P1028/T1 gap report: hook-agent-depth-comparison.md, Gap 2\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c5ddc46cd0543cee1d32df15b9eb39d1221f578e985b46274aaa44d15f27c95a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS7Xwg\"}"}